{"y":2000,"label":"1999–00","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":25,"l":10,"cw":10,"cl":6,"confFinish":"4th in Big East","finish":"r32","seed":5,"region":"South","apPre":1,"apHigh":1,"apFinal":20,"srs":16.93,"sos":7.58,"ortg":109.3,"drtg":95.6,"pace":68.2,"ppg":74.6,"oppg":65.3,"story":{"headline":"Defending Champs, Early No. 1","text":"The defending champions opened 1999–2000 ranked No. 1 and beat No. 10 Duke and No. 2 Arizona early. Khalid El-Amin, now the leader, averaged 16.0 points, earned first-team All-Big East honors, became a Naismith Award finalist and set a Big East record by making 93.4 percent of his free throws in league play; his career-high 34 points came in a 75–70 home loss to Notre Dame on January 5 that snapped a 10-game winning streak. UConn went 25–10 (10–6 Big East) and reached the Big East tournament final with wins over Boston College, Seton Hall and Georgetown before St. John's won the title game 80–70. In the NCAA tournament the Huskies beat Utah State 75–67, then fell to Tennessee 65–51 in the second round. El-Amin and Voskuhl went back-to-back to the Chicago Bulls in the 2000 draft.","moments":[{"date":"2000-03-11","title":"Big East tournament Championship: L vs St. John's","text":"UConn lost to St. John's 70–80 (Championship) at Madison Square Garden, New York, NY."},{"date":"2000-03-17","title":"NCAA First Round: W vs Utah State","text":"UConn beat Utah State 75–67 in the NCAA tournament first round at BJCC, Birmingham, AL."},{"date":"2000-03-19","title":"NCAA Second Round: L vs Tennessee","text":"UConn lost to Tennessee 51–65 in the NCAA tournament second round at BJCC, Birmingham, AL."}],"honors":["Khalid El-Amin – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1999%E2%80%932000_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khalid_El-Amin"]},"roster":[{"pid":"khalid-el-amin-1","name":"Khalid 